Some things are inaccessible to scripting, namely:
* `ScriptServer` which can be used to list supported languages to be displayed in the manager (UPDATE: linking a PR which helps to implement this on the scripting side: godotengine/godot#40147)
* `ScriptLanguage` is not exposed to scripting either to generate default templates:

```cpp
virtual Ref<Script> get_template(const String &p_class_name, const String &p_base_class_name) const = 0;
virtual void make_template(const String &p_class_name, const String &p_base_class_name, Ref<Script> &p_script) {}
virtual bool is_using_templates() { return false; }
```

So partially it's doable, but do users really have to suffer the lack of usability of the built-in feature already present in core?
